
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.GetMassMKS(): number`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`float llGetMassMKS();`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns a float that is the mass (in Kilograms) of object that script is attached to. Functionally identical to <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetMass" target="_blank">llGetMass</a> except for the unit used in the return value.</p>
  <p><b>MKS</b> as used in the name of this function is likely a reference to the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MKS_system_of_units" target="_blank">MKS system of units</a> (Meter, Kilogram, Second), which form the base of SI units (with some minor differences).</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>linkset</li>
        <li>physics</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">382</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Attachments do not effect an avatar's mass, only certain Appearance settings.
    <ul>
      <li>Avatar mass is reported to either be unexpectedly low (when measured using <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetMass" target="_blank">llGetMass</a>) or unexpectedly high (when measured using llGetMassMKS). This is likely due to the weight being calculated based on a fixed value, with a modifier for height. The fixed value being used is incorrect, likely due to an incorrect density value being used.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`--Reports an object's mass in Lindograms and Kilograms.
function LLEvents.touch_start()
    local undefined = #events
    ll.Say(0, "My weight in Lindograms: " .. tostring(ll.GetMass()) .. "\nMy weight in Kilograms: " .. tostring(ll.GetMassMKS()))
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//Reports an object's mass in Lindograms and Kilograms.
default
{
    touch_start()
    {
        llSay(0,"My weight in Lindograms: " + (string)llGetMass() + "\nMy weight in Kilograms: " + (string)llGetMassMKS());
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>the Kilogram value seems to be the Lindogram value multiplied by 100.</li>
  </ul>
